  "repair": "The authored carrier-local pelvis lowers before first Catch and stays bent through both Catch and Land into one absorption trough. Free-Air ankle heights approach the board earlier and asymmetric bent arms stay low and open. Baker, captured body, shared code, contact times, board path and caught shoes remain unchanged. Reference height is not subtracted twice.",
